# --- GOLDEN TEST FIXTURE (os213 — IBM OS/2 1.30.2 SE, Presentation Manager) ---
# resetMode=loadvm : the disk is a standalone qcow2; snapshot "golden" holds
# live RAM + disk, baked on the EXACT device set in qemu-streamhost.sh
# (isapc / 486 / 16 MB / isa-vga / KVM / ide-hd with AUTO geometry). Checkpoint,
# binary and device set are ONE combination — rule 6.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_GOLDEN_DISKS=os213-golden.qcow2
# Pointer: QEMU PS/2 RELATIVE. isapc has NO USB, so usb-tablet and every
# absolute route are unavailable; SH_POINTER=rel is not a shortcut here, it is
# the only transport the machine has. Motion + click are proven with
# scripts/dev/fb-react.py, not with a two-target absolute readback.
# Keyboard: fleet floor 40/40 (QEMU) — not bisected, per playbook §0.
# Network: none. OS/2 1.3 ships no TCP/IP stack, so this station is off the
# retronet and has no rn-tapnet.sh (rule 15).
# Fixture: the OS/2 1.3 Presentation Manager Desktop Manager at VGA 640x480x16
# with its group windows open; no modal dialog, no screensaver.
# Measured 2026-09-13: cold boot to the PM Desktop Manager 22.3 s; `savevm
# golden` VM_SIZE 3.21 MiB; restore through the launcher's own `-loadvm golden
# -S` + `cont` settles in 8.2 s to a byte-identical fixture.
# Keyboard PROVEN: two Down keys move the Group-Main selection, 5270 px changed.
# Pointer: relative MOTION proven (fb-react REACTION); a click does not reach
# the guest yet — OPEN, see docs/guests/os213.md.
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=os2-13-pm-desktop-manager
